<title>BRAZIL: SOCCER-BRAZILIAN SOCCER RESULTS/STANDINGS.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-BRAZILIAN SOCCER RESULTS/STANDINGS.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of midweek matches</p>
<p>in the Sao Paulo and Rio de Janeiro soccer championships:</p>
<p>Sao Paulo championship</p>
<p> America-S.J.Rio Preto   3    Portuguesa Santista	3</p>
<p> Botafogo-Ribeirao Preto 3    Uniao Sao Joao	     1</p>
<p> Guarani		     1    Rio Branco		   0</p>
<p> Juventus		    3    Internacional Limeira    3</p>
<p> Palmeiras		   1    Aracatuba		    1</p>
<p> Portuguesa		  3    Mogi Mirim		   1</p>
<p> Santos			2    Sao Paulo		    2</p>
<p>Standings</p>
<p> Group One		 P   W  D  L F  A  PTS  </p>
<p> Palmeiras		 17 10  6  1 42 19 36</p>
<p> Portuguesa		17  9  5  3 37 24 32</p>
<p> Santos		    17  8  6  3 31 21 30</p>
<p> Guarani		   17  5  7  5 32 38 22</p>
<p> Juventus		  17  3  6  8 30 38 15</p>
<p> Sao Jose		  16  2  7  7 21 33 13</p>
<p> Botafogo		  17  1  8  8 12 22 11</p>
<p> America		   17  2  4 11 14 42 10</p>
<p>Group two</p>
<p> Corinthians	     16 10  4  2 44 20 34</p>
<p> Sao Paulo		 17  6  9  2 27 17 27</p>
<p> Uniao Sao Joao	  17  6  5  6 22 20 23</p>
<p>Internacional Limeira 17  5  7  5 28 29 22</p>
<p> Rio Branco		17  5  6  6 21 24 21</p>
<p> Mogi Mirim		17  5  6  6 22 26 21</p>
<p> Aracatuba		 17  5  5  7 21 24 20</p>
<p> Portuguesa Santista   17  5  5  7 23 30 20</p>
<p>Note: The teams play once against the other teams in their</p>
<p>own group, then twice against the teams in the other group. At</p>
<p>the end of this, the top two teams in each group qualify for the</p>
<p>final play-off stage. If teams are level on points, positions</p>
<p>are decided by the number of games won.</p>
<p>Rio de Janeiro championship, second stage</p>
<p> Americano		   0   Fluminense		    2</p>
<p> Botafogo		    2   Bangu			   1</p>
<p> Vasco da Gama	     2   Madureira		     1</p>
<p>Played Tuesday</p>
<p> Volta Redonda	     1   Flamengo			3</p>
<p>Second stage standings</p>
<p> Botafogo		   5  3  2  0  7  4 11</p>
<p> Fluminense		 5  3  1  1  8  5 10</p>
<p> Vasco da Gama	    5  3  1  1  5  3 10</p>
<p> Americano		  5  2  1  2  7  7  7</p>
<p> Bangu			4  1  2  1  5  3  5</p>
<p> Flamengo		   4  1  2  1  8  7  5</p>
<p> Madureira		  5  0  3  2  6  9  3</p>
<p> Volta Redonda	    5  0  0  5  4 12  0</p>
<p>Note: the winners of the first, second and third stages</p>
<p>qualify for the final round. Only the top eight in the first</p>
<p>stage go into the second stage and the top six teams in the</p>
<p>second stage carry on into the third stage. If the same team</p>
<p>wins all three stages, they become champions automatically.</p>
<p>First stage winners - Botafogo</p>
<p>Eliminated in the first stage - Itaperuna, America, Olaria,</p>
<p>Barreira.</p>
